      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Prior to these needless changes, I could pull the trigger until it clicked and then hold it to grab a physbone and move it, my own or another person's. Then, if the physbone was poseable, I could click the grip buttons to reales it in whatever pose I had left it it (locking it's pose). I could then click my trigger on the physbone to release it's pose.\n\nNow, after this horrible update, (besides the myriad of broken bindings and atrocious movement) I can no longer do any of this. Physbones without poseable checked, I cannot interact with at all. And physbones with poseable checked simply get pushed around and the randomly lock themselves in place. On other's they don't even see it, so it's local. On myself, I have to reset avatar or release poses to get them to return to their original spot. \n\nI have tried many different bindings settings and it does not change this behavior. Please revert this update entirely for VIVE wand users or spot me the cash to buy new controllers with finger tracking that I don't like or want. It wasn't broke, and didn't need a fix. Forgive my frustrations. Thank you.\n\nUpdate: I have found that it is a very VERY specific spot on my trigger pull before it clicks to be able to grab physbones. It's so tiny that I couldn't even find it originally. Is there a way to change it back to being a click?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
