      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{63a4f088dc4eb42719adf0a6|full_name} Unfortunately, SteamVR input 2.0 isn't just a switch they can turn off for Vive controllers. In the meantime until we probably get a dedicated pose binding, you can mess with the grab & interact button binds on the trigger.\n\n- The `Grab` bind specifies when you'll pick up a world prop or physone and has a default deadzone of 25%. You can lower this~ I've reduce it to 10%\n\n- The `Interact` bind allows you to interact with world stuff but it also serves a dual purpose of triggering physbone pose when it's activated. \n\nI've made a walkthrough for fixing various binding issues like movement [in the VRC discord.](https://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/1274575331809951764/1274575369286189079) Give it a go and see if it alleviates any if your issues. If not be sure to upvote related cannies or make new ones for new issues.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
