      "value": "@{5f2e0a4e8464150716ffd322|full_name} So I can no longer use the trigger click to both interact with a world object like a button and grab a physbone. The closest I could get it is Making my trigger click grab a physbone and grip release it, but now grip is interact instead of also being trigger click. \"drop\" seems to do nothing at all.\n\nAll I want is to be able to grab a world object, click a world button, or grab a physbone with the trigger click. None of this partial pull crap. My physical grip is weak and I cannot hold the trigger half way for very long.\n\nThen I want to be able to lock a physbone and release a held object by clicking the grip buttons. Like I have been doing for the past 5 years before this update.\n\nUpdate: After way messing around with bindings for awhile, I got it so that I can click the trigger to interact, and and partial pull will grab. I had managed to set it up the original way it had worked for 5+ years, but then the triggers would not interact with world objects. For a layman like me with hand issues, this has been a frustrating nightmare. I apologize for my frustrations, but I just want the way that worked back.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
