      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hello~ \n\nJust adding my voice to this conversation. \n\nIt's so hard to keep things held without dropping them. Interacting with things with a high threshold setting feels terrible, and fully pulling the trigger while playing games is cumbersome. Lowering the Interact threshold \"fixes\" the issue for interacting, but then it's nearly impossible to hold things because you reduce the window where items are held; leading to me unable to pick things up or hold things at all.\n\nHaving the \"Interact\" button also Pose is a huge flaw. It means the \"Interact_Threshold\" must be larger than the \"Grab_Threshold\". Ideally the interact/grab threshold should be low (and the same value) for responsiveness, and Posing should be a deliberate action like a click of the trigger or grip buttons.\n\nI want to cry T_T Not being able to interact with my surroundings is such a frustrating experience. Some game worlds just don't work for me.\n\nPlease Please Please help me. I'm genuinely struggling with this, and with the current settings I can't find a solution.\n\nThank You 💛\n\nAngst!\n\nIf any Vive Wand users read this and have figured out a binding that works I would love to hear from you. Currently I have Interact set to a low threshold and \"Grab\" set to grip. This works well great for buttons and, I can still grab and pose physbones, but grip grabbing not ideal. Some game worlds and world items just do not work for me, and open_hand gesture grabbing things feels bad compared to the old ways.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
